%1 must log out of Linux and back in before this takes full effect.\n\nSD sees the change at once - its gates read /etc/group on every call, so login\nand logto will admit %1 straight away. The account's directory is owned by its\ngroup, and a Linux session carries the groups it held when it started, so until\n%1 logs in again they can be let into the account and then refused by the\nfilesystem.\n\nThe same is true of revoke, where it matters more: somebody whose grant has\nbeen taken away keeps their access to the directory until their next login,\neven though SD has already stopped admitting them.
